# Semantic git commits

Follow [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md). **Always** use Conventional Commits. Never write unstructured subjects.

Format: `<type>(<scope>): <summary>`

- Types: `feat`, `fix`, `test`, `docs`, `refactor`, `perf`, `chore`, `ci`, `build`, `style`
- Scope is the subsystem (`cli`, `controller`, `host`, `router`, …). Omit it only for repo-wide docs or chore
- Imperative, lowercase summary; ≤ 72 characters; body when the why is not obvious
- Regular `git commit` only — no DCO (`git commit -s` / `Signed-off-by`)
- Split unrelated work into separate logical commits

Examples: `feat(cli): load plugin commands from cluster catalog`, `test(router): cover ACME HTTP-01 challenge serving`
